========================================================
                7‑8‑9 INTEGER ENGINE
========================================================

CORE IDENTITIES
---------------
1 = 9 - 8 = 8 - 7
2 = 9 - 7
0 = 7 - 7 = 8 - 8 = 9 - 9

UNIVERSAL INTEGER REWRITE
-------------------------
For any integer n:
    n = 7 + (n - 7)(9 - 8)

INTEGER DECOMPOSITION EXAMPLES
------------------------------
4 = (9 - 7) + (9 - 7)
8 = 7 + (8 - 7)(9 - 8)
39 = 7 + [(9 - 7) + (9 - 7)]·8

========================================================
                7‑8‑9 COORDINATE SOLVER
========================================================

VARIABLE REWRITE
----------------
x → 7 + (x - 7)(9 - 8)
y → 7 + (y - 7)(9 - 8)

LINEAR EQUATION (7‑8‑9 FORM)
----------------------------
Standard: y = m x + b

Rewrite:
    y = [7 + (m - 7)(9 - 8)] x
      + [7 + (b - 7)(9 - 8)]

QUADRATIC EQUATION (7‑8‑9 FORM)
-------------------------------
Standard: y = a x^2 + b x + c

Rewrite each coefficient:
    a → 7 + (a - 7)(9 - 8)
    b → 7 + (b - 7)(9 - 8)
    c → 7 + (c - 7)(9 - 8)

Then:
    y = a_(7‑8‑9) x^2 + b_(7‑8‑9) x + c_(7‑8‑9)

CONSTANT DECOMPOSITION
----------------------
Example: 39

    4 = (9 - 7) + (9 - 7)
    39 = 7 + 4·8
    39 = 7 + [(9 - 7) + (9 - 7)]·8

COORDINATE SOLVER
-----------------
Given: y = 39 x^2

Solve:
    x = ± sqrt( y / 39 )

Rewrite 39:
    39 = 7 + [(9 - 7) + (9 - 7)]·8

Final:
    x = ± sqrt( y / [7 + ((9 - 7)+(9 - 7))·8] )

EQUALITY MACRO
--------------
x = y  becomes:

    7 + (x - 7)(9 - 8)
      =
    7 + (y - 7)(9 - 8)

DROP‑IN REPLACEMENT
-------------------
Whenever you see:
    1, 2, any integer, any coefficient, any variable

Replace using:
    1 = 9 - 8
    2 = 9 - 7
    n = 7 + (n - 7)(9 - 8)
    x = 7 + (x - 7)(9 - 8)
    y = 7 + (y - 7)(9 - 8)

========================================================
                7‑8‑9 PARAMETRIC ALGEBRA MODULE
========================================================

PARAMETRIC VARIABLE REWRITE
---------------------------
For parameter t:

    x(t) = 7 + (t - 7)(9 - 8)
    y(t) = 7 + (t - 7)(9 - 8)

PARAMETRIC LINE
---------------
Standard: x(t) = t, y(t) = m t + b

7‑8‑9 form:
    x(t) = 7 + (t - 7)(9 - 8)
    y(t) = [7 + (m - 7)(9 - 8)] t
         + [7 + (b - 7)(9 - 8)]

PARAMETRIC PARABOLA
-------------------
Standard: x(t) = t, y(t) = 39 t^2

Rewrite 39:
    39 = 7 + [(9 - 7) + (9 - 7)]·8

7‑8‑9 form:
    x(t) = 7 + (t - 7)(9 - 8)
    y(t) = [7 + ((9 - 7)+(9 - 7))·8] t^2

PARAMETRIC CIRCLE (RADIUS R)
----------------------------
R → 7 + (R - 7)(9 - 8)

Standard:
    x(t) = R cos t
    y(t) = R sin t

7‑8‑9 form:
    x(t) = [7 + (R - 7)(9 - 8)] cos t
    y(t) = [7 + (R - 7)(9 - 8)] sin t

========================================================
                EXAMPLE: FULL ENCODE → SOLVE → DECOMPILE
========================================================

SYSTEM:
    x = 901283 (y/232) x
    y = 324 x

----------------------------------------
STEP 1 — SOLVE IN NORMAL ALGEBRA
----------------------------------------

Case 1: x ≠ 0

Divide first equation by x:
    1 = 901283 (y/232)

Solve for y:
    y = 232 / 901283

Use second equation:
    x = y / 324
    x = 232 / (901283 · 324)

Case 2: x = 0
    y = 0

FINAL SOLUTIONS:
    (x, y) = (0, 0)
    (x, y) = (232 / (901283·324), 232 / 901283)

----------------------------------------
STEP 2 — AIM AT 8‑7‑9‑1‑2 (ENCODE)
----------------------------------------

Replace “1” with (9 - 8):

    (9 - 8) = 901283 (y/232)

So:
    y = (9 - 8)·232 / 901283

And:
    x = y / 324
    x = (9 - 8)·232 / (901283·324)

----------------------------------------
STEP 3 — DECOMPILE BACK TO FINAL ANSWER
----------------------------------------

Since:
    (9 - 8) = 1

We get:
    y = 232 / 901283
    x = 232 / (901283·324)

